{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556049-more-info-on-precolumbian-kindred","id":1556049,"title":"More info on Precolumbian Kindred","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-01T01:44:38-08:00","id":1556049,"title":"More info on Precolumbian Kindred","content":"in the writeup for the Tlacique on page 64 of <i>Lore of the Clans</i>, mention is made of<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">vampires [in the New World] already: Nosferatu, Gangrel, and a bloodline calling itself the Tlacique.</div> <br /> my assumption is that the former two are in reference to the Manitou mentioned across pages 24-25 of Revised Edition's <i>Clanbook: Nosferatu</i> and Mictlantecuhtli's (perhaps by extension the Slumbering Giant's) bloodline from <i>Diablerie: Mexico</i>, respectively. while the Tlacique have a handful of writeups to their name, these other two seem more marginal; have either been detailed anywhere outside of the aforementioned sources? are there any other (non-Drowned Legacy) bloodlines from the precolumbian Americas im missing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28978-balalyka","name":"balalyka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28978_1.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T02:52:51-08:00","id":1556052,"title":"","content":"The Tlacique were the ones that killed Melinda Galbraith, the Sabbat Regent, in 2001's Palla Grande and the big bad of South America that been teased in World of Darkness 2nd ed. Their write-up is on Blood Sacrifice: The Thaumaturgy Companion.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T06:34:53-08:00","id":1556055,"title":"","content":"None, this was essentially an abandoned thread.<br /> <br /> Even the Tlacique may actually be a Drowned Legacy, as do the other Kindred that were already there given that DLs may have the ability to pass as Kindred.<br /> <br /> In canon Masquerade Kindred are definitely a localized phenomenon despite their apparent success. If any reached the Americas before Columbus, no evidence of their passage was really found beyond a few individuals that may not actually be what they seem to be. Vampires outside the Middle East is a far newer phenomenon than previously thought by Europeans.<br /> <br /> You take from this what you will, if you want Native American Kindred you'll have to homebrew them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T07:34:25-08:00","id":1556059,"title":"","content":"The Baali<br /> They are always a safe bet, Nergal/Huitzilopochtli landed before Columbus and built a cozy little empire for himself and his brood<br /> Tezcatlipoca... was something, either a Lasombra or either Sutekh's kid, still up to the air<br /> Mictlantecuhtli and the Slumbering Giant represented the Gangrel - and it is quite possible with the Viking settlers a few <b>Einherjar </b>tagged along<br /> The Psianob are either from a Cappadocian survivor or a DL of their own right<br /> Menele came over at one point prior to the major European settlers to hang out with the natives<br /> V5 Chicago by Night introduces us to Nerissa Blackwater, a 4th generation Caitiff. She's been hunting in the Lake Michigan area since 4000 BC<br /> The mostly-torpid Tzimisce antediluvian was brought over to what would become New York by the Szantovich Revenants shortly after Lugoj's botched diablerie. That would have been at or a little after 1413... <br /> <br /> to be fair, not counting the Viking, there are evidances of the Indian (Ravnos and whatever lingered there at that time), Chineese , japan, african (Laibon) contacts - this one is reaches back to the time of the paharos actually , hell even early Chinese accounts of Muslim expeditions state that Muslim sailors reached a region called Mulan Pi that is usually belived to be spain, but more likely part of America<br /> And of course the Phoenicians reached it probably too (this one supported by why Menele knew where to go)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T17:10:27-08:00","id":1556073,"title":"","content":"The Tlacique's write up was in the revised Followers of Set Clanbook IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T01:12:57-08:00","id":1556087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556049-more-info-on-precolumbian-kindred?p=1556073#post1556073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tlacique's write up was in the revised Followers of Set Clanbook IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, teased there, expanded on Blood Sacrifice.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T04:04:40-08:00","id":1556090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556049-more-info-on-precolumbian-kindred?p=1556059#post1556059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Baali<br /> They are always a safe bet, Nergal/Huitzilopochtli landed before Columbus and built a cozy little empire for himself and his brood<br /> Tezcatlipoca... was something, either a Lasombra or either Sutekh's kid, still up to the air<br /> Mictlantecuhtli and the Slumbering Giant represented the Gangrel - and it is quite possible with the Viking settlers a few <b>Einherjar </b>tagged along<br /> The Psianob are either from a Cappadocian survivor or a DL of their own right<br /> Menele came over at one point prior to the major European settlers to hang out with the natives<br /> V5 Chicago by Night introduces us to Nerissa Blackwater, a 4th generation Caitiff. She's been hunting in the Lake Michigan area since 4000 BC<br /> The mostly-torpid Tzimisce antediluvian was brought over to what would become New York by the Szantovich Revenants shortly after Lugoj's botched diablerie. That would have been at or a little after 1413...<br /> <br /> to be fair, not counting the Viking, there are evidances of the Indian (Ravnos and whatever lingered there at that time), Chineese , japan, african (Laibon) contacts - this one is reaches back to the time of the paharos actually , hell even early Chinese accounts of Muslim expeditions state that Muslim sailors reached a region called Mulan Pi that is usually belived to be spain, but more likely part of America<br /> And of course the Phoenicians reached it probably too (this one supported by why Menele knew where to go)</div> </div> </div> </div>Tezcatlipoca was unofficially a Tlacique (Setite) who happened to know &quot;Cry That Slays Light&quot; ritual according to one of the Revised era writers. He is featured in Mexico City by Night.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T05:25:41-08:00","id":1556094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556049-more-info-on-precolumbian-kindred?p=1556052#post1556052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tlacique were the ones that killed Melinda Galbraith, the Sabbat Regent, in 2001's Palla Grande and the big bad of South America that been teased in World of Darkness 2nd ed. Their write-up is on Blood Sacrifice: The Thaumaturgy Companion.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really find any source where it is stated the Tlacique slained Melinda Galbraith before a Palla Grande in 2000<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary gave a few options who might been Galbraith's assassins: the Inquisition or Assamites and even teased the possibility that she faked her own Final Death at the command of her master, Nergal/Huitzilopochtli <br /> <br /> But found no mention the Tlacique did the deed (as a side note, personally I don't think it would make sense they did it; Nergal/Huitzilopochtli, the Baali and the Pisanob ruled basically together with the Tlacique - and if you dip in to extended splash, even the Balam and some shapeshifters took part in this nice arrangement - not really would make sense for them to remove Huitzilopochtli's pawn in a very important position eg. the head of the Sabbat who arguably one of the last possible allies they might have if no other options available ; sure they not necesarily knew who Galbraith's true master was, but still, they knew the Sabbat is not a Dragon but a multi-headed Hydra and removing the Regent means pretty much nothing; they are regularly owerthrown be another in every 100 years or so - Mind's Eye Theatre even listed all the Ragents in its continuity <br /> Also she posed as a Lasombra and again, Tezcatlipoca was a very important figure in that alliance of vampires ruling the area with heavy Lasombra traits; not to mention the Tlacique themselves are said to be descended from Him...<br /> Again, something they not necesarily knew<br /> But anyway, things just don't add up)<br /> <br /> Could you please help out with a reference, they did it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T23:33:20-08:00","id":1556115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556049-more-info-on-precolumbian-kindred?p=1556090#post1556090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tezcatlipoca was unofficially a Tlacique (Setite) who happened to know &quot;Cry That Slays Light&quot; ritual according to one of the Revised era writers. He is featured in Mexico City by Night.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer the official stuff, but not against such unofficial thing - for example the Assamite history that left out from their revised book is one of my favorite<br /> Thematically of course it makes sense Tezcatlipoca was Sutekh's kid that ended up in the other side ofthe globe either tagging along with traders who crossed the ocean or simply shadow-stepped there<br /> A 4th Generation Settite knowing Obtenebration and Abyss mysticism is totally viable, considering the level 9 Sperentis power <b>Shadow of Apep </b>allows you to become a nearly indestructible giant snake of pure darkness and <b>Pact with Ra</b> let you walk in the sun without harm for one day<br /> Yet the Tlacique are descended from Tezcatlipoca and what they don't have? Serpentis and Obtenebration... but have protean and their own unique brand of magic, <b>Nahuallotl</b> <br /> Interestingly, they call one of the path they know Rites of Tezcatlipoca their version of Spirit Manipulation witch is fitting, considering their connection to the local Shifters<br /> But basically no connection to the Darkness their progenitor commands<br /> So either they failed to inherit as a bloodline the defining trait of their Father (strange) and developed their own brand, this Tezcatlipoca\u200b is not <i>their</i> Tezcatlipoca... or they simply really a seperate breed, a DL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T13:58:26-08:00","id":1556134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556049-more-info-on-precolumbian-kindred?p=1556115#post1556115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I prefer the official stuff, but not against such unofficial thing - for example the Assamite history that left out from their revised book is one of my favorite<br /> Thematically of course it makes sense Tezcatlipoca was Sutekh's kid that ended up in the other side ofthe globe either tagging along with traders who crossed the ocean or simply shadow-stepped there<br /> A 4th Generation Settite knowing Obtenebration and Abyss mysticism is totally viable, considering the level 9 Sperentis power <b>Shadow of Apep </b>allows you to become a nearly indestructible giant snake of pure darkness and <b>Pact with Ra</b> let you walk in the sun without harm for one day<br /> Yet the Tlacique are descended from Tezcatlipoca and what they don't have? Serpentis and Obtenebration... but have protean and their own unique brand of magic, <b>Nahuallotl</b><br /> Interestingly, they call one of the path they know Rites of Tezcatlipoca their version of Spirit Manipulation witch is fitting, considering their connection to the local Shifters<br /> But basically no connection to the Darkness their progenitor commands<br /> So either they failed to inherit as a bloodline the defining trait of their Father (strange) and developed their own brand, this Tezcatlipoca is not <i>their</i> Tezcatlipoca... or they simply really a seperate breed, a DL</div> </div> </div> </div>I never liked it either, to me he was always a Lasombra.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}